  <h3 data-slot="title">A fraction</h3>
  <div data-slot="question">
    <p class="at-lab">Question</p>
    <p>Use the rule <i>y</i> = <i>x</i><sup>2</sup> to find <i>y</i> when <i>x</i> = 3/2.</p>
  </div>
  <hr class="at-hr">
  <div data-slot="steps">
    <p class="at-lab">Worked solution</p>
    <ol class="at-steps">
      <li class="at-step"><div class="at-st">Substitute. The whole fraction is squared, not just the numerator.</div><div class="at-sm"><i>y</i> = (3/2)<sup>2</sup></div></li>
      <li class="at-step"><div class="at-st">Square the top and the bottom.</div><div class="at-sm"><i>y</i> = 3<sup>2</sup>/2<sup>2</sup> = 9/4</div></li>
      <li class="at-step"><div class="at-st">Squaring a value above 1 makes it larger; this one lands just above 2.</div><div class="at-sm">9/4 = 2.25</div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div data-slot="answer"><b>Answer</b><i>y</i> = 9/4, so (3/2, 9/4) lies on the graph.</div>
